# Configuration Guide

This project has three main configuration files:

```text
.env               private Bybit keys and deployment values; never commit it
docker-compose.yml starts the QKT daemon container
qkt.config.yaml    QKT runtime behavior and Bybit broker profile
```

## .env

Start with testnet:

```dotenv
QKT_IMAGE_TAG=v{{QKT_VERSION}}
BYBIT_TESTNET=true
BYBIT_API_KEY=
BYBIT_API_SECRET=
```

`BYBIT_API_KEY` and `BYBIT_API_SECRET` come from Bybit. Use restricted API keys
and testnet first. Set `BYBIT_TESTNET=false` only when you intentionally want to
connect to real funds.

Optional alerts:

```dotenv
TELEGRAM_ENABLED=false
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
```

## docker-compose.yml

Compose starts one `qkt` service. There is no separate gateway container because
QKT talks to Bybit REST directly through the configured broker.

## qkt.config.yaml

The broker block points QKT at Bybit. Strategy files should use the configured
broker path and let QKT handle order/risk/accounting flow.

Keep risk limits explicit before using real funds. Testnet passing is not proof
that a strategy is safe for live money.

## State

QKT writes runtime state under `./state`. Keep it when you care about deployed
strategy state, reconciliation, or restart recovery.

